    description: { en: 'Knockouts compress weeks into days — how to keep client work shipping through the closing stretch of World Cup 2026 with an AI-assisted workflow that protects the matches.', fr: 'Les phases finales compressent les semaines — comment continuer à livrer les clients pendant la fin de la Coupe du Monde 2026 avec une IA qui protège les matches.', es: 'Las eliminatorias comprimen las semanas — cómo seguir entregando a clientes durante el cierre del Mundial 2026 con un flujo IA que protege los partidos.', pt: 'As eliminatórias comprimem semanas — como manter a entrega para clientes no fecho do Mundial 2026 com um fluxo IA que protege os jogos.', it: 'I quarti comprimono settimane in giorni — come continuare a consegnare ai clienti nel finale del Mondiale 2026 con un workflow IA che protegge le partite.', de: 'K.-o.-Runden komprimieren Wochen — wie du im Endspurt der WM 2026 Kundenarbeit lieferst, mit KI-Workflow, der Spiele schützt.', pl: 'Faza pucharowa zagęszcza tygodnie — jak dowozić zlecenia w końcówce MŚ 2026 z workflowem AI chroniącym mecze.' },
    faq: [
      { q: 'How do knockouts change my work week?', a: 'Match cadence picks up dramatically and emotional bandwidth drops on result days. Front-load deep work to mornings before matches, batch client comms into two short windows daily, and protect post-final days as recovery — not "make-up the missed week" days.' },
      { q: 'Which AI workflows save the most hours right now?', a: 'A capable assistant that drafts emails, summarises meeting recordings, and turns rough voice notes into client-ready text compresses a day’s output into half the time. The freelancers shipping through the tournament are using AI as a first pass, not as the deliverable.' },
      { q: 'What about client expectations?', a: 'Set them in writing once. A single calendar block named "deep work — limited replies" at fixed hours signals professionalism, not absence. Clients respect explicit availability far more than vague always-on noise that drops at unpredictable moments.' },
      { q: 'How do I avoid the post-final crash?', a: 'Schedule one quiet day after the final for nothing, then walk into the week with a pre-set Monday brief and three small wins lined up. The slump is real; pre-loading momentum beats trying to summon it after the noise of the closing weekend.' },
    ],
